---
name: "Fix PR Checks"
description: "Fixes failing GitHub PR checks"
tags: [integrate, pr-checks]
stage: integrate
---

## Context

`mohist/merge-github-pr` rejected the merge because one or more GitHub PR checks
failed for PR #`${{ failure.output.prNumber }}` (`${{ failure.output.prUrl }}`).
The merge action is waiting on you to repair the checks before it can squash-merge.

The previous failure surfaced a structured `failure.output.message` describing
which checks failed; read that as the entry point.

## Process

1. Inspect the PR check status for the affected PR:
   ```bash
   gh pr view ${{ failure.output.prNumber }} --json statusCheckRollup \
     --jq '.statusCheckRollup[] | {name, status, conclusion, detailsUrl}'
   ```
2. For every check whose `conclusion` is `FAILURE` / `ERROR` / `CANCELLED` /
   `ACTION_REQUIRED`, identify the failing job.
3. Use `gh run view <run-id>` / `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed` to fetch
   the failing job's logs and pinpoint the root cause.
4. Apply focused fixes to source code, tests, or build configuration so that
   the affected checks would pass on the next run. Prefer correcting code or
   tests over weakening assertions.
5. Stage and commit the fixes on the workflow branch.
6. Do not push from this task. The workflow will run the explicit
   `recover:push` task after this repair completes.

## Rules

- Do NOT reopen or recreate the PR. Reuse the same workflow branch and the
  same open PR (`${{ failure.output.prNumber }}`).
- Do NOT mark the PR ready again — `merge-github-pr` only checks PR state,
  not PR readiness. Committing the fix is enough; `recover:push` handles sync.
- Do NOT modify the merge action's behavior. Recovery is scoped to making
  the existing PR's checks pass.
- Do NOT run `git push`; branch synchronization is an explicit workflow task.
- You may be interrupted at any time: commit incrementally and keep your progress
  notes current.

## Output

```markdown
## Applied PR Check Repairs
- PR #<number> check: <name> — root cause and fix summary

## Verification
- Local build/test/typecheck command run and result
- Commit created on `${{ workspace.branch }}`
```
